{"h":3390,"lines":[{"t":"G","x":0.082135523348785641,"y":0.48401162797098229,"w":0.020533881187438957,"h":0.014534883302221635,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"Reading","y":0.044100901308510743,"w":0.081232833862304621,"h":0.015912081288025348,"x":0.83524149306931372},{"h":0.016224188790560423,"w":0.75359344482421875,"x":0.12320327752100639,"c":1,"y":0.091445427555196135,"t":"The damage starts when logging companies arrive to clear the trees. They dig ditches to"},{"y":0.10856482099161047,"w":0.78248433430989583,"t":"enter the peat swamps by boat and then float the logs out the same way. These are then used","h":0.018453844458656055,"x":0.12725003134739096,"c":1},{"h":0.017499314367243723,"c":1,"x":0.12731006849737042,"w":0.77412729899088562,"y":0.12645348818023905,"t":"to drain water out of the peatlands to allow for the planting of corn, oil palms or pulpwood"},{"h":0.018872209847149213,"x":0.12724049829190107,"y":0.1438379902261836,"w":0.76193720499674478,"t":"trees. Once the water has drained away, bacteria and fungi then break down the carbon in","c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.12731007269466421,"w":0.75154001871744802,"y":0.16279069769716792,"h":0.017445290264478497,"t":"the peat and turn it into CO2 and methane. Meanwhile, the remainder of the solid matter"},{"y":0.17572543828498244,"w":0.63086171468098962,"c":1,"t":"in the peat starts to move downwards, in a process known as subsidence**","h":0.024620483758526879,"x":0.1271026835391435},{"t":"Peat comprises","x":0.74266584090639076,"y":0.17768089803593701,"h":0.021930420011897267,"c":1,"w":0.15520105997721345},{"w":0.77425394694010419,"x":0.12723360927921998,"c":1,"y":0.19733481252831209,"t":"90 per cent water, so this is one of the most alarming consequences of peatland clearances.","h":0.019643854461940058},{"h":0.016038965545924322,"c":1,"w":0.77618067423502612,"t":"'In the tropics, peat subsides at about four centimetres a year, so within half a century, very","x":0.12731007343729164,"y":0.21651917386866781},{"t":"large landscapes on Sumatra and Borneo will become flooded as the peat drops below water","y":0.23326836608942114,"w":0.78655522664388022,"h":0.01826556157925141,"x":0.12725471158607585,"c":1},{"h":0.017699115044247815,"y":0.25132743346834663,"t":"level,' says Silvius. 'It's a huge catastrophe that's in preparation. Some provinces will lose","c":1,"w":0.77207392374674466,"x":0.12525667250939299},{"t":"40 per cent of their landmass.'","x":0.12707504103893513,"h":0.019441677757420783,"w":0.26344548543294272,"c":1,"y":0.26877624133806255},{"x":0.12320328279213527,"h":0.017481305957895432,"w":0.70636550903320305,"c":1,"t":"And while these industries affect wetlands in ways that can easily be documented,","y":0.30523255815163819},{"h":0.017984603499241025,"t":"Dr Dave Tickner of the WWFN believes that more subtle impacts can be even more","x":0.12723591016480745,"c":1,"y":0.32125600053065884,"w":0.71676905314127604},{"c":1,"t":"devastating. 'Sediment run-off and fertilisers can be pretty invisible,' says Tickner.","x":0.12731006238962703,"w":0.70636550903320305,"y":0.34011627940952271,"h":0.018895347842776244},{"w":0.78039906819661453,"c":1,"t":"'Over-extraction of water is equally invisible. You do get shock stories about rivers running","x":0.12725856938138047,"h":0.020187152873801684,"y":0.35703725746759341},{"w":0.7560073343912761,"h":0.024721554106315713,"c":1,"x":0.12509482860557322,"t":"red, or even catching fire, but there's seldom one big impact that really hurts a wetland.'","y":0.37206695885680641},{"w":0.76180699666341145,"x":0.12731005393805428,"h":0.01605697339263279,"t":"Tickner does not blame anyone for deliberate damage, however. 'T've worked on wetland","y":0.39528023578954463,"c":1},{"h":0.019328717707181142,"x":0.1252086484697143,"y":0.41116728639219779,"c":1,"t":"issues for 20 years and have never met anybody who wanted to damage a wetland,' he says.","w":0.78653203328450516},{"x":0.12731006702656372,"y":0.43008849538916749,"w":0.77412729899088539,"t":"'It isn't something that people generally set out to do. Quite often, the effects simply come","c":1,"h":0.017699115044247815},{"h":0.021938465759817505,"y":0.44610336577628251,"c":1,"x":0.12706111618756286,"t":"from people trying to make a living.'","w":0.32090777079264321},{"y":0.48255813934302982,"t":"Silvius also acknowledges the importance of income generation. 'It's not that we just want","c":1,"x":0.11498975598866404,"h":0.017441860412777732,"w":0.78644760131835945},{"c":1,"t":"to restore the biodiversity of wetlands - which we do - but we recognise there's a need","w":0.74537989298502605,"y":0.50145348848370541,"h":0.015988371857499573,"x":0.12525666549690415},{"w":0.76404378255208338,"c":1,"y":0.5173784627058472,"h":0.020362743726522137,"t":"to provide an income for local people.' This approach is supported by IWMI.iThe idea is","x":0.12721797412404784},{"y":0.53775811185609435,"x":0.12731007346855269,"w":0.7761806742350259,"c":1,"h":0.017474446254493903,"t":"that people in a developing country will only protect wetlands if they value and profit from"},{"c":1,"y":0.55368731591631204,"w":0.75770019531249999,"h":0.018987102002169132,"t":"them,' says McCartney. 'For sustainability, it's essential that local people are involved in","x":0.12731006482834972},{"t":"wetland planning and decision making and have clear rights to use wetlands.'","x":0.12719887265517721,"w":0.66353230794270845,"c":1,"h":0.021347781831184354,"y":0.57116037082684878},{"t":"The fortunes of wetlands would be improved, Silvius suggests, if more governments","x":0.12731005261320091,"y":0.60901162802093178,"w":0.72073923746744795,"h":0.016062118170183992,"c":1},{"w":0.77633010864257801,"h":0.020591936139582101,"x":0.12721320713899265,"y":0.6246977666678889,"c":1,"t":"recognised their long-term value. 'Different governments have different attitudes,' he says,"},{"y":0.6438953488499618,"w":0.73716634114583313,"c":1,"h":0.017461583185336527,"x":0.12731005343750829,"t":"and goes on to explain that some countries place a high priority on restoring wetlands,"},{"w":0.77220169067382816,"y":0.66105648826419428,"h":0.019291603741040886,"c":1,"t":"while others still deny the issue. McCartney is cautiously optimistic, however. 'Awareness","x":0.12724963498987865},{"h":0.0174598682594862,"w":0.76796712239583331,"x":0.12731007263165206,"c":1,"t":"of the importance of wetlands is growing,' he says. 'It's true that wetland degradation still","y":0.67876106172887929},{"t":"continues at a rapid pace, but my impression is that things are slowly changing.'","h":0.020126795135768094,"w":0.68604054768880207,"y":0.69618272193576447,"c":1,"x":0.12722070426462589},{"t":"** subsidence: the sinking of the Earth's surface, most often caused by the removal of resources from the ground","w":0.67145792643229163,"h":0.01179941002949858,"y":0.89675516213543272,"x":0.086242289247919837,"c":1},{"t":"67","h":0.014534883302221635,"c":1,"x":0.88911704407607395,"w":0.028747431437174509,"y":0.91860465122679613},{"w":0.45294118245442705,"y":0.94166666659226195,"c":1,"h":0.04166666666666663,"t":"IELTSXpress.com","x":0.51176470218665204}],"w":2400}